  "scope": "Whole-graph registration coordination under native graph admission and transaction ownership; memory conflicts/capacity/insertion and SQLite record/capacity/quota/conflict/write/watermark/consuming commit order.",
  "limitations": [
    "Frozen registration bodies share native admission, bounded codecs, capacity/quota/storage and watermark primitives, not migrated orchestration.",
    "Memory bounded-image checks precede conflicts and capacity. Infallible trusted-owner writes preserve their original prefix on unwind; no memory rollback or new low-level request admission is claimed.",
    "SQLite encodings are exact native buffers in admitted branch order. Group duplicate registration is a conflict, never replay or repair; branch write errors retain original native diagnostics.",
    "The 192 SQLite matrix cases use three representative operations and parallel/sequential orders, not all 70 durable operation combinations. Twelve additional production group-start shapes cover result bindings and reserved successors.",
    "Disposable corrupt fixtures restore constraints before production calls. Raw filler rows probe record limits; a virtual oversized view probes quota refusal without physical disk-full. These are not admitted checkpoints.",
    "Direct hooks model fault/unwind including uncertain commit; real triggers and deferred constraints probe rollback. No process-kill, power-loss or multi-physical-host test is claimed.",
    "Public-start failure leaves caches empty and rolls back the graph, but sequence reservations committed earlier by the root allocator are not refunded. Only an explicit subsequent start retries.",
    "No new Linux, remote CI, live GUI, standalone exported-source execution, full host-neutral durable recovery or throughput benchmark is claimed."
  ],
